# Skill router

Read this entry point at the start of each work request, before opening task skills. Plain conversation needs no routing. Reuse an unchanged copy already in context; re-route when the task changes.

## Select, load, work

1. Identify the requested result, task scope, and any named skill, service, or framework. For a known or named project, consult its row in [project and agent routing](project-routing.md) to select relevant skills and a suitable agent brief. Follow explicit skill requests and mandatory prerequisites.
2. Choose the matching route below. Consult only its linked catalog when the choice needs more detail; compare neighboring alternatives by their selection criteria.
3. Load the selected skill's `SKILL.md` and required companions before doing the work. Add a companion when it covers a distinct required part of the task. Similar descriptions alone are not a reason to load several skills.
4. Follow only the selected skill's relevant branches and references. Stop discovery once the task is covered. State the chosen skills briefly, then complete the work.

Choose by task fit, not familiarity. A recommendation is a scope-based starting point, not a quality benchmark. Reconsider the route when new evidence changes the task.

