  35: 2. Pass fixtures for actual-rate updates, Euler rejection before mutation, learning-off invariance, APL equivalence/current matching, certificate semantics, frozen rankings and atomic recovery.
  36: 3. Freeze the complete checkpoint schedule, R control interpretation, seeded tapes, fresh sealed data, collision/exclusion rules, metrics and exact pass/resource budgets.
  37: 4. Obtain strict code-review clearance; complete the bounded informative dry run and its independent audit before full confirmation.
  38: 
